module bindings.javascript.oauthQueryAccessTokenUntyped;

// RFC 6750 offers a bearer client three transports for the access token: the
// Authorization header, a form-encoded body parameter, and the URI query
// parameter -- and its own guidance recommends against the last, because URIs
// leak through logs and referrers. A token taken from the query string has a
// second property the header does not: its value is built by a query parser,
// and a parser lets the requester choose the runtime type. Bracket syntax
// (`?access_token[$ne]=null`) parses to the object `{'$ne': 'null'}`, which is
// truthy, satisfies any `if (!token)` presence check, and reaches a NoSQL
// equality lookup on the token as an operator rather than a literal -- so a
// match no longer means the requester held the token. A TypeScript annotation
// on the parameter cannot pin it: the cast that bridges the request object to
// the annotated record type is exactly where the lie lives. What pins it is a
// runtime scalar check where the value is extracted: `typeof x === 'string'`,
// or an equivalent validation call.
//
// The function-scope shape read here uses the protocol's own vocabulary only:
// the routine strips a `Bearer ` prefix (the RFC's header option) in the same
// function that reads a `query.access_token` member (the RFC's query option,
// under the parameter name it defines), and carries no `typeof` check. Both
// conjuncts are needed: a function may legitimately parse bearer headers, and
// a function may legitimately read query parameters; taking the documented
// token from the documented query spelling while also doing bearer-header
// authentication is what makes this the credential path. Nothing
// project-specific is named, so any OAuth implementation that accepts both
// documented transports and skips the scalar check reports the same finding.
binding oauthQueryTokenScalarCheckMissing {
  query pattern presenceNode where node.scope == "function" and node.context.language == "javascript" and node.context.literal contains "Bearer " and node.context.selector contains "query.access_token" and not (node.context.expr contains "typeof")
  emit issue code.OauthQueryTokenScalarCheckMissing at node
}
